      "dom_id": "question-44931",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "What is the $5$th term of the arithmetic sequence \n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-5,\\,{a}_{1}=3,\\,n\\ge 1?\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Starting with the first term ${a}_{1}=3,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive rule until we reach the $5$th term ${a}_{5}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =3 \\\\ {a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}-5=3-5=-2 \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={a}_{2}-5=-2-5=-7 \\\\ {a}_{4} & ={a}_{3}-5=-7-5=-12 \\\\ {a}_{5} & ={a}_{4}-5=-12-5=-17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $5$th term is ${a}_{5}=-17.$",
